<figure class="cache-figure" data-restore-freshness>
 <p class="figure-title">Restoring bytes does not make their contents younger</p>
 <p class="figure-note">Source observed: 12 at 0 s · snapshot: 20 s · source changes to 15 at 30 s · Redis stops at 40 s</p>
 <div class="cache-controls"><label>Restore at <input data-time type="range" min="50" max="110" step="1" value="70" /> <output data-time-label>70 s</output></label><label><input data-age type="checkbox" /> Enforce a 60 s source-observation age limit</label></div>
 <div class="restore-timelines"><div><span>Saved key expiry · 90 s</span><div class="restore-track"><i style="width:75%"></i><b data-marker></b></div></div><div><span>Application age limit · 60 s</span><div class="restore-track"><i style="width:50%"></i><b data-marker></b></div></div><div class="restore-axis"><span>0 s · observed</span><span>120 s</span></div></div>
 <div class="recovery-pair"><div class="recovery-node"><b>Restored Redis entry</b><strong data-entry></strong><small data-ttl></small></div><div class="recovery-node"><b>Application decision</b><strong data-decision></strong><small data-age-label></small></div></div>
 <p class="explanation" data-explanation aria-live="polite"></p>
 <figcaption>The marker is the restore time; both bars use the same 0–120 s scale. The saved entry includes its original expiry and source-observation timestamp. The optional age check is application logic, not a Redis TTL feature. It bounds permitted age, not equality with the latest source value. Clocks are assumed stable and sufficiently aligned.</figcaption>
</figure>
<script>
import{restoredCache}from'../../lib/caching/recovery.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-restore-freshness]').forEach(root=>{const time=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-time]')!,age=root.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-age]')!;const render=()=>{const s=restoredCache(Number(time.value),age.checked);root.querySelector('[data-time-label]')!.textContent=`${s.time} s`;root.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-marker]').forEach(el=>el.style.left=`${s.time/120*100}%`);root.querySelector('[data-entry]')!.textContent=s.present?'12':'Empty';root.querySelector('[data-ttl]')!.textContent=s.present?`${s.ttl} s of TTL remain`:'Original expiry has passed';root.querySelector('[data-decision]')!.textContent=s.accepted?'Return 12':'Load source';root.querySelector('[data-age-label]')!.textContent=`Source observation is ${s.age} s old`;root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=!s.present?'The saved expiry was 90 s. Recovery does not grant another 90 seconds: the key is absent.':!s.accepted?'The key still exists, but its observation is too old for the application’s contract. Reject it and use the bounded source-loading path.':`The key is present and the application accepts it. It returns 12 while the source holds 15.${age.checked?' The observation is inside the chosen age limit; that is not a promise of the latest value.':' A surviving TTL alone does not establish freshness.'}`;};time.oninput=render;age.onchange=render;render();});
</script>
